    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-i/q9-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A curve C  has implicit equation 3 2 ax − 3 xy + by = 224 , where a and b are non zero constants. The normal to the curve at the point ( ) P − 2,6 has equation 15 x − 13 y + 108 = 0 . Determine the value of a and the value of b . ( 12 )\" style=\"--madas-width:577.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-i/q9-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:582.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-i/q9-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Using (−2, 6) in the equation gives −8a + 36 + 36b = 224, [M1] [A1] so −8a + 36b = 188, or −2a + 9b = 47. [M1] [A1] Rearrange 15x −13y + 108 = 0 to 13y = 15x + 108, i.e. y = (15/13)x + 108/13. The normal gradient is 15/13, so the tangent gradient is −13/15. [M1] [A1] Implicit differentiation gives 3ax2 −3y + (−3x + 2by)y′ = 0. [M1] [A1] Substituting x = −2, y = 6, y′ = −13/15 [M1] gives 12a −18 + (6 + 12b)y′ = 0, hence y′ = (18 −12a)/(6 + 12b) . = (3 −2a)/(1 + 2b) Therefore the normal gradient is (2b + 1)/(2a −3) = 15/13. Cross-multiplication gives\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-i/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"13(2b + 1) = 15(2a −3), 26b + 13 = 30a −45, 30a −26b = 58. Dividing by 2 gives 15a −13b = 29. [A1] Multiply the first point equation by 15 and the gradient equation by 2. Adding −30a + 135b = 705 and 30a −26b = 58 gives 109b = 763, so b = 7. Then −2a + 63 = 47, hence −2a = −16. Thus a = 8, b = 7 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 9 is 12 marks.</p>"
