    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-i/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A pension broker gets paid £15commission per week for every pension scheme he sells. Each week he sells a new pension scheme so that … In the st 1 week he gets paid £15commission for the pension he just sold. nd week he gets paid £30 , £15 for the pension sold in the st In the 2 1 week plus £15 nd for pension he sold in the 2 week. rd week he gets paid £45, £15 for the pension sold in the st In the 3 1 week plus £15 nd rd for pension he sold in the 2 week, plus £15 for the pension he sold in the 3 week, and so on. a) Find the commission he gets paid on the last week of the year. ( ) 2\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-i/q10-question-2.svg\" alt=\"b) Find his annual earnings after one year in this job. ( ) 2 nd His commission increases to £20 for new pension schemes sold during the 2 year but decreases to £10 for the schemes he sold in the st 1 year. The broker continues to sell at the rate of one new pension scheme every week. nd ( ) 6 c) Find his annual earnings in the 2 year.\" style=\"--madas-width:588.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
