    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-i/q12",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-i/q12-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A water tank has the shape of a hollow inverted hemisphere with a radius of 1 m . It can be shown by calculus that when the depth of the water in the tank is h m , its 3 volume, V m , is given by the formula 1 2 V = π h ( 3 − h ) . 3 3 Water is leaking from a hole at the bottom of the tank, in m per hour, at a rate proportional to the volume of the water left in the tank at that time. a) Show clearly that\" style=\"--madas-width:558.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-i/q12-question-2.svg\" alt=\"dh kh ( 3 − h ) = − , dt 3 2 ( − h ) where k is a positive constant. ( ) 5 The water tank is initially full. b) Solve the differential equation to show further that ( ) 9 2 3 2e kt − 3 h − h = .\" style=\"--madas-width:589.5px\"></figure>",
